    "https://www.newcastle.edu.au/engage/career-ready-placements": {
      "title": "Career-ready placements",
      "description": "Career-ready placements - Engage - The University of Newcastle Skip to content Our thoughts are with those who are affected by the devastating disaster in Nepal. Students requiring support can access support services here and staff can visit this page for information about our Employee Assistance Program . For emergency consular assistance information, please click here . The University of Newcastle, Australia Study Undergraduate Postgraduate International Admissions and Entry Pathways PhD and Research Masters New Students Scholarships Research Research impact Research stories Partner with us Institutes and centres Research facilities Graduate Research Research support Engage Alumni Business and industry Career-ready placements School and community programs Community partnerships Global Engagement Make a gift Volunteer Development projects Campus Life Newcastle Central Coast Sydney Tamworth Singapore Accommodation Respect Help on campus University Galleries Our Uni Strategic Plan Indigenous commitment Equity, Diversity and Inclusion Sustainability Our Stories Campuses and locations Colleges and Schools Our rankings Governance and leadership Jobs Library Students Staff 0 Degree comparison tool Add degrees to wishlist 0 Degree comparison tool Search Search Menu Career-ready placements Connect with our talented and engaged students whose ideas and energy are shaping the future. Connect with us How it works Types of placements Placement essentials Diversify your workforce Success stories Information for students What are career-ready placements? Career-ready placements mean real on-the-job experience for our students. These powerful experiences happen in partnership with industry, community, and government. It helps our students forge strong relationships that prepare them not only for their future workplace, but also for life after they graduate. How it works If you are interested in hosting a student on placement, we will work closely with you throughout the placement cycle, providing support and resources along the way. Learn more Types of placements Career-ready placements are discipline-specific and take many forms. Learn more Placement essentials Everything you need to know about timing, supervision, health and safety, intellectual property, insurance, and more. Learn more Get connected to our talented students. Start here. Interested in being part of our career-ready placement program? Get in touch and we can discuss your career-ready placement opportunity. This form will be received by our industry engagement staff who will respond within two days to your enquiry. We will contact you to discuss your opportunity further or connect you directly with the staff member who will be managing your placement. Connect with us to get started Area of Interest -- Please Select -- General enquiries and/or multiple areas of interest Architecture and Construction Management Arts and Social Sciences Biomedical Science Biotechnology Business, Marketing, HR, Entrepreneurship, Analytics, and International Business Commerce, Finance, Economics, and Accounting Computer Science, Data Science and IT Education Engineering and Surveying Environmental Science and Development Studies Food Science and Human Nutrition Global Indigenous Studies Health and Medicine Law and Criminology Mathematics Media and Communication Performing and Creative Arts Psychology Science Social Work Software Engineering Tourism, Hospitality and Events Other (please specify) I agree to the Privacy Policy of University of Newcastle Submit Thank you! One of our representatives will respond soon Sending your details... Diversify your workforce Learn how career-ready placements can help you to foster diversity and inclusion in the workplace. Learn more Success stories Discover how our industry partners have helped our students realise their potential—and how our students’ ideas and energy have helped host organisations realise theirs. Learn more More ways to engage Employ a student or graduate Businesses need talented people who are ready to make a difference and we know that finding the right people can be challenging. We can support your search for talent. Read more Join us on campus Attending Careers events and expos is a cost-effective way for you to connect with your future workforce and promote your organisation. We can also facilitate employer information sessions and employer presentations for you to speak directly to our students. Read more Connect with our research Knowledge Exchange and Enterprise (KEE) connects industry with the University's world-class research and technologies. Read more Email us Email us Call (02) 4921 5588 Call us Connect with us Complete online form The University of Newcastle acknowledges the traditional custodians of the lands within our footprint areas:  Awabakal, Darkinjung, Biripai, Worimi, Wonnarua, and Eora Nations. We also pay respect to the wisdom of our Elders past and present. Quick links Degrees Library Maps Staff directory Canvas MyUni Online tools AskUON The Shop Information about Our Uni Strategic Plan Colleges and schools Campus life Jobs Make a gift Community partnerships Indigenous commitment Emergency and security Information for Research Business and Industry International students Alumni Current students Current staff News Media 中文(简体） Got a question? AskUON Connect with us Facebook Instagram TikTok LinkedIn Youtube WeChat Weibo Little Red Book The University of Newcastle, Australia © 2026 Contact us Copyright and Disclaimer Privacy Accessibility ABN 15 736 576 735 CRICOS Provider 00109J TEQSA Provider ID PRV12056 (Australian University) Back to top Are you visiting our site from South Asia ? Head to our dedicated page with all the information you need to study at the University of Newcastle. Close 您是否在中国访问我们的网址？ 前往 专属页面 ，查询你在纽卡斯尔大学学习所需的所有信息。 Close Library Students Staff Close Home Study Research Engage Campus Life Our Uni Study Undergraduate Where to start Find a 