    "https://www.newcastle.edu.au/our-uni/jobs": {
      "title": "Be part of research that’s changing lives",
      "description": "Jobs at the University of Newcastle / Our Uni / The University of Newcastle, Australia Skip to content Our thoughts are with those who are affected by the devastating disaster in Nepal. Students requiring support can access support services here and staff can visit this page for information about our Employee Assistance Program . For emergency consular assistance information, please click here . The University of Newcastle, Australia Study Undergraduate Postgraduate International Admissions and Entry Pathways PhD and Research Masters New Students Scholarships Research Research impact Research stories Partner with us Institutes and centres Research facilities Graduate Research Research support Engage Alumni Business and industry Career-ready placements School and community programs Community partnerships Global Engagement Make a gift Volunteer Development projects Campus Life Newcastle Central Coast Sydney Tamworth Singapore Accommodation Respect Help on campus University Galleries Our Uni Strategic Plan Indigenous commitment Equity, Diversity and Inclusion Sustainability Our Stories Campuses and locations Colleges and Schools Our rankings Governance and leadership Jobs Library Students Staff 0 Degree comparison tool Add degrees to wishlist 0 Degree comparison tool Search Search Menu Be part of research that’s changing lives We are looking for people to join our university - to bring your global expertise to our regions, and to take your powerful ideas to the world with us. Current vacancies Benefits Indigenous employment Joining us from overseas Why join the University of Newcastle Our vision to become a world-leading university for our regions will take passion and perseverance. Our regions are important to us. We were literally built, brick-by-brick, by our community more than fifty years ago. And our community - our students - remain at the heart of every decision we make. Collaboration is in our DNA. It’s one of the reasons we’re the number one university in the world for partnering for a sustainable future, and number one in Australia for industry collaboration. Top 10 ? university in Australia for Graduate Employability Top 1% ? university in the world WGEA ? Employer of Choice for Gender Equity, five years in a row 5-star ? maximum rating for social equity Current vacancies We have a range of academic and professional roles available in diverse fields across the institution. Internal Vacancies View positions External Vacancies View positions Reasonable Adjustments We are committed to equity, diversity and inclusion and as such, hope to increase the representation of staff with disability across all levels of academic and professional roles. If you are applying for a job with us, have a disability and require an adjustment to be made to the recruitment process, we encourage you to reach out for support. We are determined that every applicant has the best opportunity to demonstrate their talents, skills and suitability for a role. However, please know that you are not obligated to disclose disability if you do not feel ready. Gender-based Violence Prevention We are committed to a safe, respectful and inclusive community. In line with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence, we consider Gender-based Violence (GBV) risk factors in recruitment. GBV includes physical or non-physical violence or abuse driven by harmful beliefs about gender. All applicants must complete the University’s GBV Declaration, which asks only about past GBV investigations or findings involving conduct by the applicant. Applicants are not required to disclose experiences as a victim/survivor. Employment offers remain conditional pending a confidential review. Find out more Diverse and Inclusive Workplace Equity is in our DNA. We know that embedding equity, diversity and inclusion as the guiding principles in all we do helps us to live and achieve our other values of excellence, engagement and sustainability. Find out more Indigenous Commitment We are proud to be a sector leader in Indigenous employment, education, and research. We prioritise the embedding of Indigenous knowledge across the University to nurture an awareness of issues and a strong commitment to social justice. Find out more SAGE Athena Swan We are proud to be one of the first two Universities in Australia to achieve SAGE Athena Swan Silver Accreditation for gender equity, diversity, and inclusion (GEDI). This is an international award that reflects our ongoing efforts in this area. Find out more Our stories Hippocampus A shift in energy With 17 Hunter Valley mines set to close over the next 20 years, the region is facing a significant turning point. Conversations often centre around job losses, but what comes next for those who will remain? Read more Hippocampus The secret lives of Sugarloaf koalas “Tree stars” in the night sky revealed a hidden koala colony, nestled deep within Sugarloaf’s bushland. Read more Hippocampus This uni program is changing the game for mob From one students’ first time in a classroom to a mum-of-three’s return to learning, these real-life stories show what’s possible when universities open doors and open minds. Read more Show more stories Hippocampus Where learning meets care The University of Newcastle’s community clinics are providing life-changing services and transforming the wellbeing of 5,000 people a year. Read more Hippocampus Teaching the Hunter Eric Roach was just 19 when he graduated from Newcastle Teacher's College in 1953. His time there launched a career that would span almost four decades, and instilled in him a passion for teaching that would transcend generations. Read more Hippocampus “I thought I was a bad mother”: How telehealth changed a young boy’s life and gave a family hope “I thought I was a bad mother,” says Marlie Matthews, tearfully. “I tried everything, but Marcus was getting more and more behind. He wasn’t speaking much and when he did, I couldn’t understand him. It was very hard on all of us.” Read more Show more stories Looking Ahead Strategic Plan 2030 We are a University of our regions and for our regions. The spirit of looking to the future to imagine and then realise possibilities is at the essence of our strategic plan. Learn more Coming from overseas We are a modern and growing region that is forging a bright new future. You get the best of Australian life but with the added benefit of a unique mix of space and everything on your doorstep. Read more Organisational structure Led by the Vice-Chancellor and President, our University is organised around academic Colleges and Schools and professional Divisions. Read more The University of Newcastle acknowledges the traditional custodians of the lands within our footprint areas:  Awabakal, Darkinjung, Biripai, Worimi, Wonnarua, and Eora Nations. We also pay respect to the wisdom of our Elders past and present. Quick links Degrees Library Maps Staff directory Canvas MyUni Online tools AskUON The Shop Information about Our Uni Strategic Plan Colleges and schools Campus life Jobs Make a gift Community partnerships Indigenous commitment Emergency and security Information for Research Business and Industry International students Alumni Current students Current staff News Media 中文(简体） Got a question? AskUON Connect with us Facebook Instagram TikTok LinkedIn Youtube WeChat Weibo Little Red Book The University of Newcastle, Australia © 2026 Contact us Copyright and Disclaimer Privacy Accessibility ABN 15 736 576 735 CRICOS Provider 00109J TEQSA Provider ID PRV12056 (Australian University) Back to top Are you visiting our site from South Asia ? Head to our dedicated page with all the information you need to study at the University of Newcastle. Close 您是否在中国访问我们的网址？ 前往 专属页面 ，查询你在纽卡斯尔大学学习所需的所有信息。 Close Library Students Staff Close Home Study Research Engage Campus Life Our Uni Study Undergraduate Where to start Find a degree Admissions and entry 