    "https://www.newcastle.edu.au/our-uni/jobs/job-vacancies/collection-statement": {
      "title": "The University Of Newcastle Collection Statement",
      "description": "Collection Statement / Job vacancies / Jobs at the University of Newcastle / Our Uni / The University of Newcastle, Australia Skip to content Our thoughts are with those who are affected by the devastating disaster in Nepal. Students requiring support can access support services here and staff can visit this page for information about our Employee Assistance Program . For emergency consular assistance information, please click here . The University of Newcastle, Australia Study Undergraduate Postgraduate International Admissions and Entry Pathways PhD and Research Masters New Students Scholarships Research Research impact Research stories Partner with us Institutes and centres Research facilities Graduate Research Research support Engage Alumni Business and industry Career-ready placements School and community programs Community partnerships Global Engagement Make a gift Volunteer Development projects Campus Life Newcastle Central Coast Sydney Tamworth Singapore Accommodation Respect Help on campus University Galleries Our Uni Strategic Plan Indigenous commitment Equity, Diversity and Inclusion Sustainability Our Stories Campuses and locations Colleges and Schools Our rankings Governance and leadership Jobs Library Students Staff 0 Degree comparison tool Add degrees to wishlist 0 Degree comparison tool Search Search Menu Homepage Our Uni Jobs at the University of Newcastle Job vacancies Collection Statement Our Uni Our Uni Strategic Plan - Looking Ahead 2030 Indigenous Commitment Sustainability Equity, Diversity and Inclusion Campuses and locations Governance and leadership Jobs at the University of Newcastle Job vacancies Application process Collection Statement Coming from overseas? Rankings Contact Us Admissions Transparency Venues and Events NUServices Our Uni The University Of Newcastle Collection Statement This Collection Statement sets out how your personal information will be collected, managed and protected in relation to recruitment opportunities and activities, including appointment, and onboarding processes where applicable. If you are successful in securing a position at University of Newcastle ( we, us or our ), personal information collected during the recruitment process will form part of your employment record. This information will be managed in accordance with the relevant Privacy Management Plan . The Privacy Management Plan includes additional information about how information is collected, used, disclosed, and managed in relation to employees. Collecting your personal information Humanforce Holdings Pty Ltd at Level 10, 90 Arthur Street North Sydney, NSW, 2060 Australia (Humanforce Talent ) will be collecting your personal information on our behalf when you apply for a role with us. Personal information will be requested and collected at registration and as part of the recruitment process. If you do not have a Humanforce Talent Profile, one will be created for you as part of the online application process, using your personal information that you provided as part of that online application process. This means that we and Humanforce Talent may use your personal information to contact you about future job opportunities with us as part of our Talent Community. Personal information collected may include your name, contact details, career history, qualifications, skills, training, working with children checks if relevant, and psychometric profiles. Information will also be collected during interview processes. We rely on the personal information you provide to be complete, up to date, accurate and truthful. If you provide any false or misleading information, we may disqualify your application and/or if appointed, terminate your employment without notice. We may also collect information from other parties where relevant, including: licensing authorities. appointed selection panel and hiring managers. In some cases, a recruitment activity may require meeting with, or providing a job talk to, a selected group of key staff. The input of those staff may also be considered as part of the recruitment process. Where this may be required, candidates will be informed as part of the recruitment processes. internet or social media searches, including job search or professional networking websites (e.g. LinkedIn, etc.) where you may have made data about yourself publicly available. previous employers. recruiters, staffing companies, or websites who may introduce or direct you to us. police and agencies who provide background checks where applicable. Resume databases. testing providers. We may also contract with a third party to perform pre-employment background screening and employment references. The content of background check information may include information gathered from publicly available sources, your former employers or colleagues, educational institutions you have attended, credit reporting agencies, and criminal records databases. If you do not provide your personal information we require, this may limit our ability to provide you with relevant information about job opportunities, recruitment activities, answer your queries, or process your employment application. Where you provide details of referees, it is your responsibility to ensure that these persons are aware that you have forwarded their details and have consented for you to do so. We may request more detailed personal information from you, on a voluntary basis, to assist us to provide support and services to disadvantaged equity groups and create equity candidate pools. Where a position has been identified or targeted by us, (to address under-representation or as a result of an inherent role requirement) the provision of additional relevant personal information may be considered mandatory. We may also request additional information, such as gender, for non-identified roles. This is for reporting purposes. Using your personal information Your personal information will be used: to administer and manage your registration. to communicate with you about your application to work with us. to communicate with you more generally about working with us, any employment searches and/or queries you may have regarding recruitment processes. This includes communicating with you about future employment opportunities if you have consented. to manage and assess your application, interview, and suitability for employment. for quality improvement, planning, and reporting activities in relation to recruitment, appointment, and onboarding processes where relevant. This may including data analytics that can improve the university’s recruitment processes and help us better understand our applicants to support how the university may attract the best candidates. Sourcing candidates for future employment opportunities To ensure we attract the best candidates, we may consider and use publicly available information and contact individuals directly who may be considered suitable for a recruitment activity. This collection statement will apply to the subsequent collection and management of any information collected by us as a result of this contact. Disclosing your personal information We may provide personal information where relevant, to contracted third parties to facilitate recruitment processes. This may include: recruitment agencies and Executive Search firms referees background checking agencies licensing authorities and educational institutions in order to verify information about you psychological profiling and background screening services. providers of relevant information systems and services. companies providing video interviewing and interview assessment services. testing providers. We use contracted third parties to assist us in providing systems and services that are relevant to the recruitment and appointment of staff. We take reasonable steps to ensure that these organisations have compliant privacy procedures in place and are only allowed to use your personal information to assist us in undertaking our recruitment activities. We will not disclose your personal information to a third party outside the scope of this notice or without your consent, except where required or authorised by law. Managing your personal information Access to your information is restricted only to our authorised personnel and contracted third parties on a need-to-know basis. Any personal information held by us will be treated in the strictest confidence. We are committed to taking all reasonable steps in order to protect your privacy and personal information from misuse, loss or unauthorised access, modification or disclosure. Your information will be retained in accordance with our retention procedures and legislated obligations, and to support opportunities for employment, collaboration or engagement with us. Further Information You can contact our Human Resource Services Unit in relation to this privacy statement or make a request by writing to the Chief People & Culture Officer, University of Newcastle, University Drive, Callaghan NSW 2308, or by contacting the Talent Acquisition team at employment@newcastle.edu.au . Further information about how we manage privacy, including how to make a complaint please contact the Privacy and Rights to Information Officer, at privacy@newcastle.edu.au . The University of Newcastle acknowledges the traditional custodians of the lands within our footprint areas:  Awabakal, Darkinjung, Biripai, Worimi, Wonnarua, and Eora Nations. We also pay respect to the wisdom of our Elders past and present. Quick links Degrees Library Maps Staff directory Canvas MyUni Online tools AskUON The Shop Information about Our Uni Strategic Plan Colleges and schools Campus life Jobs Make a gift Community partnerships Indigenous commitment Emergency and security Information for Research Business and Industry International students Alumni Current students Current staff News Media 中文(简体） Got a question? AskUON Connect with us Facebook Instagram TikTok LinkedIn Youtube WeChat Weibo Little Red Book The University of Newcastle, Australia © 2026 Contact us Copyright and Disclaimer Privacy Accessibility ABN 15 736 576 735 CRICOS Provider 00109J TEQSA Provider ID PRV12056 (Australian University) Back to top Are you visiting our site from South Asia ? Head to our dedicated page with all the information you need to study at the University of Newcastle. Close 您是否在中国访问我们的网址？ 前往 专属页面 ，查询你在纽卡斯尔大学学习所需的所有信息。 Close Library Students Staff Close Our Uni Home Study Research Engage Campus Life Our Uni Study Undergraduate Where to start Find a degree Admissions and entry Key dates and events Accommodation Scholarships Parents and teachers Study Postgraduate Flexible study Degrees and programs Credit Fees and costs How to apply Key dates Study International Study with us How to apply Fees and costs Before you leave Life in Australia While you are here The University in your country 关于纽卡斯尔大学 Study Pathways Open Foundation Yapug Diplomas NUPrep Bridging and Refresher Courses Newcastle International College (NIC) English Language Pathways (formerly ELICOS) Study PhD and Research Masters Future research students Current research students Supervisors Examiners Industry and community About graduate research Forms, guidelines and policies HDR FAQs Study New Students Accepting your offer Plan your degree Enrol Prepare for university Placement Orientation Home Study Undergraduate Postgraduate International Admissions and Entry Pathways PhD and Research Masters New Students Scholarships Research Research stories Research impact Our researchers Research Partner with us NIER HMRI Knowledge Exchange and Enterprise (KEE) Integrated Innovation Network (I2N) Defence capabilities TUNRA Hire a graduate Research Institutes and centres NIER HMRI Research Research facilities Central Analytical Facilities Research Research support Research services Research systems Home Research Research impact Research stories Partner with us Institutes and c